Subject: [PATCH] 1048 redfin: keep the console chunk a failed send could not deliver

ud_log_thread() called sweet_log_copy() straight into the stream position, and
sweet_log_copy() advances that position. So when sock_send() failed - which it
does for every chunk until 192.168.7.1 exists, since the host has to add the
address by hand after enumeration - the chunk was gone: the next call started
after it. The boot backlog was dropped exactly when it was wanted, which is why
every capture began at "exec xpcproxy" and none ever contained SWEET FB or the
mount of the iOS root.

Copy into a candidate position and commit it only after the send returns 0, so
the same bytes are retried until one gets through.
---
diff --git a/bsd/dev/sweet_usb.c b/bsd/dev/sweet_usb.c
index 74ad9a6..fb0a7bc 100644
--- a/bsd/dev/sweet_usb.c
+++ b/bsd/dev/sweet_usb.c
@@ -1461,7 +1461,19 @@ ud_log_thread(void *arg __unused, wait_result_t wr __unused)
 			continue;
 		}
 		uint32_t n, burst = 0;
-		while ((n = sweet_log_copy(&pos, chunk, sizeof(chunk))) > 0) {
+		while (1) {
+			/*
+			 * Copy into a candidate position and only commit it once the send
+			 * succeeded: sweet_log_copy advances its cursor, so a failed send
+			 * used to drop that chunk for good. At boot the thread starts
+			 * before 192.168.7.1 exists (the host adds it by hand), so every
+			 * backlog chunk failed and the boot log was lost.
+			 */
+			uint64_t next = pos;
+			uint32_t n = sweet_log_copy(&next, chunk, sizeof(chunk));
+			if (n == 0) {
+				break;
+			}
 			struct iovec iov = { .iov_base = chunk, .iov_len = n };
 			struct msghdr msg = {
 				.msg_name = &to, .msg_namelen = sizeof(to),
@@ -1469,8 +1481,9 @@ ud_log_thread(void *arg __unused, wait_result_t wr __unused)
 			};
 			size_t sent = 0;
 			if (sock_send(so, &msg, 0, &sent) != 0) {
-				break;          /* no route/ARP yet: retry later */
+				break;          /* no route/ARP yet: retry this chunk later */
 			}
+			pos = next;
 			if (++burst % 32u == 0) {
 				ud_sleep_ms(5);  /* pace a large backlog */
 			}
